<%
  content_for :page_title, "Advanced Search | #{domain_name}"
%>

<%# The test id lets controller tests tell this page from the index and the
    form, which share its URLs, without pinning how the login control works. %>
<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6" data-testid="saved-searches-intro">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Advanced Search</h1>

  <p>
    Build a search the quick filters can't express, and keep it. You can narrow by:
  </p>

  <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
    <li>Fiction or nonfiction</li>
    <li>Book length</li>
    <li>Publication years</li>
    <li>Ranked books only, or just the top N</li>
    <li>Genres, subjects and settings to include or exclude, matched with AND or OR</li>
    <li>Languages to include or exclude</li>
    <li>Countries of origin to include or exclude</li>
    <li>Hiding books you've read</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Save a search to come back to it later. Saving needs a free account.
  </p>

  <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" onclick="login_modal.showModal()">Login</button>
</div>
